<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Costanera Q3 net up to $12.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Costanera Q3 net up to $12.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to September 30</p>
<p>Net $12.7 million vs $8.8 million</p>
<p>Nine months</p>
<p>Net $38.3 million vs $29.8 million</p>
<p>Shr $0.28 vs $0.22</p>
<p>ADR $2.8 vs $2.2</p>
<p>Revs $243.4 million vs $231.5 million</p>
<p>NOTE: the company did not provide EPS, ADR or revenues for the third quarter.</p>
<p>At September 30 its net worth stood at $377.3 million and retained earnings at $51.2 million.</p>
<p>Central Costanera SA, Argentina's largest thermoelectric generating company, is controlled by a consortium headed by Chile's ENDESA.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
</text>
